FreeRTOS port pinned sources
---------------------------

Scope:

  ports/freertos-nrf52833/platform.lock.yml

Nothing under ports/freertos-nrf52833/ vendors third-party code. That lock file
pins the repositories and revisions the port compiles and links against; the
sources are fetched into a workspace outside this repository, so no glob here
matches a file in the tree. The list below maps each pinned component to its
license so an audit of a built image has one place to start.

  Apache NimBLE (apache/mynewt-nimble)
    the BLE host, its FreeRTOS porting layer, and its syscfg defaults
    License: Apache-2.0, in the Apache License 2.0 section below

  Nordic MPSL and SoftDevice Controller (nrfconnect/sdk-nrfxlib)
    linked as binary libraries, with their headers compiled
    License: LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause, in the Nordic section above

  Nordic nRF 802.15.4 service layer (nrfconnect/sdk-nrfxlib)
    libnrf-802154-sl.a and the platform headers this port implements
    License: LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause, in the Nordic section above

  Nordic sources compiled unmodified from nrfconnect/sdk-nrf
    subsys/bluetooth/controller/hci_internal.c
    modules/nrfxlib/nrf_802154/sl/platform/nrf_802154_hp_timer.c
    modules/openthread/platform/radio_nrf5.c
    License: LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause, in the Nordic section above

  nrfx and the nRF 802.15.4 driver (zephyrproject-rtos/hal_nordic,
  nrfconnect/sdk-nrfxlib)
    the peripheral HAL and the 802.15.4 driver core
    License: BSD-3-Clause, in the BSD 3-Clause section below

  OpenThread (nrfconnect/sdk-openthread)
    the Thread stack
    License: BSD-3-Clause, in the BSD 3-Clause section below

  Mbed TLS (nrfconnect/sdk-mbedtls)
    the crypto provider, built standalone with its PSA core; the port supplies
    only its configuration, its threading callbacks, its allocator, and its
    entropy source
    License: Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later, at the user's choice. This
    project takes it under Apache-2.0, in the Apache License 2.0 section below.

    Nordic's nrf_oberon is deliberately NOT pinned and is not part of any built
    image. It carries LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause, the same restriction this
    port already accepts for MPSL and the SoftDevice Controller, so adopting it
    later would add no new one -- but until it is adopted, the crypto in this
    port is Apache-2.0 and redistributable on its own terms.

The Nordic license permits binary redistribution only as embedded in a Nordic
Semiconductor integrated circuit, so an image built from this port carries that
hardware restriction in addition to the Qorvo one stated above.

The Qorvo DW3_QM33_SDK archive that supplies the board and UWB base for this
port is a separate vendor artifact, also pinned in that lock file and also not
vendored here. Its terms are the Qorvo ones stated above.

Not a pinned component, but stated here because the name appears in the source:
ports/freertos-nrf52833/board/log_rtt_freertos.c implements a SEGGER RTT
control block from the published format. No SEGGER code is copied, compiled, or
linked, and SEGGER's own RTT implementation is licensed for use with SEGGER
products only, which is why it is not used. The identifier string it writes is
the one a J-Link scans for; SEGGER and J-Link are trademarks of SEGGER
Microcontroller GmbH, used here only to name the interface.

